"""Persian copy for every error the API can return.

The clients cannot write this themselves. A problem-details body carries a
machine code (`title`) and an English `detail` written for an operator reading
logs; both frontends were reaching for a `message_fa` that no handler had ever
sent, so every failure they could not classify rendered as generic copy - and
on the sign-in screen a wrong password rendered as "your session expired",
which sends an operator to look for a problem that is not there.

Voice matches `presentation/bot/ui/text.py`: second-person plural, say what
happened and what to do next, never "خطایی رخ داد". Codes with no entry fall
back to `GENERIC`, which is correct for the ones a client can never provoke.
"""

